# UI: match existing input widths

No full-width inputs on desktop except inside an already-narrow container (modal, sidebar, stack with `maw`).

**Before adding a field, find and reuse an existing width pattern.**

1. Search similar screens for `maw=`, `max-width`, form wrappers (Management: `Box maw={560}`; auth: `maw={400}`; short selects: `maw={240}`).
2. Wrap the group in that cap. Do not stretch to the main pane.
3. Short selects and numeric fields stay narrow; labels/help fill the capped column.
4. `w="100%"` inside a capped container is fine — still cap the container on desktop.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<TextInput label="Column label" value={label} onChange={…} />

// ✅ GOOD
<Box maw={560}>
  <TextInput label="Column label" value={label} onChange={…} />
</Box>
```
